legion (0.8.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Portability fixes adopted from the community macOS port: tool processes
    never inherit Legion's stdin (katana and httpx no longer hang), nmap plans
    leave OS detection out when raw sockets are unavailable instead of failing
    (NMAP_PRIVILEGED / NMAP_UNPRIVILEGED are honoured and the dropped detection
    is logged), the nmap HTML stylesheet is found under Homebrew too, katana
    uses the repeated -kf form and a crawl cap, the loggers no longer create a
    cache directory at import, tool paths default to names resolved from PATH
    (ntlmrelayx defaults to impacket-ntlmrelayx with a fallback to the installed
    variant) and exec-in-shell works without getent.
  * Removed the last `six` imports; the package no longer depends on
    python3-six. SQLAlchemy 1.4 through 2.1 are supported and the SQLite engine
    pins its connection pool so Save As behaves the same on both.
  * Removed an embedded Shodan API key from scripts/python/pyShodan.py and the
    unused pyshodan-api-key entry from legion.conf (the Shodan integration key
    lives in the scheduler settings, the keyring or SHODAN_API_KEY).
  * flake8 and pip-audit moved to requirements-dev.txt.

 -- Shane Scott <sscott@shanewilliamscott.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 21:48:47 +0000

legion (0.8.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Remove the Qt desktop UI; `legion` now starts the web interface and the
    package no longer depends on PyQt6, qasync or X11 libraries. The headless
    CLI and MCP server are unchanged.
  * Web UI: sortable, filterable tables; toasts and confirmation dialogs;
    bulk host actions and batch tool runs; scan re-run; import dialog with
    browser uploads for nmap XML, .gnmap and masscan XML/JSON/list reports;
    Open Workspace picker with rename and delete; executions, findings, plan
    preview and command-family policy views; richer Host Detail; light theme;
    remembered filters and paths; Font Awesome bundled for offline use.
  * Exports cover the whole project (every table as CSV or JSON) instead of
    the capped UI snapshot.
  * Security: optional web token (--web-token / LEGION_WEB_TOKEN) with a login
    page, required automatically when binding all interfaces; cross-site and
    DNS-rebinding requests are rejected; API errors are always JSON.
  * Scheduler: brute-force nmap scripts and unsafe script arguments are
    classified as risky, blocked candidates are never re-admitted, approvals
    re-check policy before running, and the evidence-graph sync, approval and
    execution stores are indexed and skip unchanged state.
  * Headless CLI: --discovery and --staged-scan run the configured stages,
    plus --nmap-args, --nmap-xml and --project.
  * MCP server speaks the MCP protocol over stdio with 32 tools.
  * Many fixes in the web runtime, importers, parsers, configuration loading
    and database cleanup; see CHANGELOG.txt.

 -- Shane Scott <sscott@shanewilliamscott.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 19:49:24 +0000

legion (0.7.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Fix the desktop UI failing to start and segfaulting on exit, and stop
    nmap import errors from aborting the application; queue overlapping
    imports and fail malformed or missing XML imports instead of reporting
    success.
  * Fix data loss around Save As (replace prompt, refused saves discarding
    the project, temporary projects saved onto their own path, importers and
    running scans following the reopened project) and around CVE replacement
    on partial vulners re-scans.
  * Fix per-host reports leaking other hosts' findings and credentials, the
    detection-risk policy having no effect, and approval lookups matching
    the wrong approval.
  * Harden process handling (kill reporting, stale PIDs, interrupted rows,
    queue slots and timers), web runtime output handling and batching,
    scheduler provider retries and caches, graph upserts and pruning, and
    importer/CLI behaviour; load Exploit-DB data offline.
  * Expand the regression suite to 937 tests and restore missing fixtures.

 -- Shane Scott <sscott@shanewilliamscott.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500

legion (0.7.0-0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Continue the web-first replatform by splitting routes into domain modules,
    adding service/schema boundaries, and shrinking the monolithic WebRuntime
    into focused runtime modules for projects, scans, scheduler, workspace,
    graph, reports, artifacts, processes, and settings.
  * Harden high-risk execution and control paths, including bind-all handling,
    public tool execution, approval idempotency, MCP state contracts, and local
    secret-store backed provider credential storage.
  * Improve project bundle export/restore fidelity, restore staging, restored
    path rebasing, artifact handling, and damaged legacy project behavior.
  * Add service/open-port filtering, graph filtering tied to host filters,
    service port visibility, stronger OS enrichment, and expanded device
    categorization for phone and out-of-band management systems.
  * Add bundled pipettes for Cisco Smart Install, internal SMTP/SPF review,
    Windows SMB/RDP discovery, and IPMI/iDRAC/iLO discovery.
  * Improve Nmap output isolation, screenshot target handling, process/tool
    execution paths, artifact cleanup, Responder/NTLMRelay workspace handling,
    and cross-surface regression coverage.

